# SRG-APP-000920-AU-000410  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must synchronize system clocks within and between
# systems or system components.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000920-AU-000410
group:           V-263584
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004922
control_rev5:    SC-45

contribution:    Splunk has no NTP client, so its share is to bound and act on clock
                 divergence between its own components, refusing to register a search peer
                 beyond addpeer_skew_limit and warning beyond max_tolerable_skew, and to
                 remove time zone ambiguity from event timestamps with props.conf TZ and
                 TZ_ALIAS.

governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.

check:           limits.conf [search] addpeer_skew_limit present
check:           limits.conf [search] max_tolerable_skew present

external:        The host operating system's time service (NTP or chrony), which is where
                 the Central Log Server SRG itself places time synchronization when the log
                 server application has no NTP client (SRG-APP-000086-AU-000030 check text)
external:        The authoritative time source shared with the host and with the devices in
                 scope of coverage
external:        Forwarder and sending device clocks, which set the event timestamps Splunk
                 records; props.conf TZ is left unset where the time zone of the host
                 running splunkd or the forwarder-supplied zone is the intended source
                 (props.conf.spec:580-590)
external:        Operating system and network device STIGs, which carry the synchronization
                 requirement for those components

citation:        SRG-APP-000920-AU-000410 check text; SRG-APP-000086-AU-000030 check text;
                 limits.conf.spec:493-502, 529-536; props.conf.spec:580-612
finding:         Splunk expresses no clock skew bound between its own components
                 (limits.conf [search] addpeer_skew_limit or max_tolerable_skew is not
                 available in the assessed configuration), so divergence between the search
                 head and its peers is neither refused nor reported.
